ign's response to McCain featured; scenes shown from Philadelphia.  [OBAMA&nbsp- says we can rebuild Philadelphia; acknowledges McCain tried to tone down his rhetoric; speaks about the economy.]  Standings of Obama and McCain in a new \"Newsweek\" poll cited.  [Pennsylvania Governor Ed RENDELL&nbsp- campaigns.]  \n\n(Studio: Lester Holt)  Tomorrow's \"Meet the Press\" mentioned. ", "segment_duration": 380, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63050.0", "legacy_segment_id": 907747, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "V8yK5qvWG2", "broadcast_date": "2008-10-11", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1730, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 907746, "segment_id": "KpfZVDgxs6", "segment_broadcast_id": "V8yK5qvWG2", "segment_title": "Economy: Financial Crisis", "segment_description": "(Studio: Lester Holt)  Report introduced.   (White House: Kevin Corke)  President Bush's plans to rescue the US financial system by cooperating with global powers featured; scenes shown of him with the G-7 leaders; details given about the bailout, efforts to free up the credit market and from the G-7 economic agreement.  [BUSH&nbsp- says we will resolve this crisis and the world's economy will emerge stronger.]  [Former IMF economist Simon JOHNSON&#134;- outlines what the European countries need to do.]  [Peterson Inst. for International Economics director C. Fred BERGSTEN&#134;- says the odds are the country will put together national plans.]  Bush's attendance at the Group of 20 meeting to send an image that the international community is coming together noted.   (Studio: Lester Holt)  How the domestic economy is being affected introduced.   (Studio: 